p: .
t: I am pleased to write the foreword to the second edition of
From Madness to Mutiny


--- Sentence/switch
i: 3
r# 143

p: .
t:  I practiced family law for twenty-five years before
transitioning to academia, where I continue my representation of abuse
survivors


--- Sentence/switch
i: 4
r# 278

p: .
t:  Most of my family law cases involved intimate partner abuse


--- Sentence/switch
i: 5
r# 340

p: .
t: 
During my academic career I have taught students to practice law in a
clinical setting, where students provide counsel to survivors of intimate
partner abuse


--- Sentence/switch
i: 6
r# 499

p: .
t:  I teach courses related to intimate partner abuse, as well


--- Sentence/switch
i: 7
r# 560

p: .
t: 
My experience working with survivors of intimate partner
abuse is significant


--- Sentence/switch
i: 8
r# 640

p: .
t:  And my alarm over what has happened in the field, particularly
over the past twenty years, is disconcerting

--- Sentence/end 
i: 8
