p: .
t: Having been involved in the field of family law for over forty years,
I have observed the backlash against women and other survivors after they made gains in protections against their abusers


--- Sentence/switch
i: 20
r# 2324

p: .
t:  These gains
were primarily in the form of civil protections orders and legislation that limited the ability of someone with a history of domestic
violence from being awarded custody of children


--- Sentence/switch
i: 21
r# 2520

p: .
t:  These gains were
short lived


--- Sentence/switch
i: 22
r# 2551

p: .
t:  Not long after statutory protections for abused partners
were implemented, angry men began organizing against women


--- Sentence/switch
i: 23
r# 2669

p: .
t:  The
so-called Fathers' Rights groups, which organize against women, particularly mothers, are not to be confused with Responsible Fatherhood
initiatives


--- Sentence/switch
i: 24
r# 2824

p: .
t:  Non-abusive, non-misogynist men do not pose concern


--- Sentence/switch
i: 25
r# 2878

p: .
t: 
This book addresses the tactics used by men who abuse intimate
partners and their children


--- Sentence/switch
i: 26
r# 2970

p: .
t:  These Fathers' Rights groups are well
funded and well organized


--- Sentence/switch
i: 27
r# 3040

p: 
t:  Another reason these men and their tactics have been successful is because typically the abusive parent has
access to more financial resources and is able to retain counsel and
experts.

--- Sentence/end 
i: 27
r# 3234

--- Paragraph/end 
i: 4
y: N/A


--- Paragraph/start
i: 5
r# 3262


--- Sentence/start
i: 28
r# 3262

p: .
t: 
Anti-victim tactics are successful in court because they are based on
negative stereotypes of women


--- Sentence/switch
i: 29
r# 3363

p: .
t:  Prevailing attitudes toward women include the idea that women lie, and, particularly, they lie about abuse


--- Sentence/switch
i: 30
r# 3476

p: .
t: 
Moreover, women who say what abusers or others do not want to hear,
are labeled some version of crazy. The pathologization of women, particularly mothers, is common and unwarranted


--- Sentence/switch
i: 31
r# 3662

p: .
t:  Pathologizing women
has a long history in our country where noncompliant women have been
institutionalized


--- Sentence/switch
i: 32
r# 3771

p: .
t:  As you will read, alternatives to institutionalization are
part of the current dismissal of women's narratives


--- Sentence/switch
i: 33
r# 3884

p: .
t:  For example, one
threat made to mothers is that unless they comply with court ordered
therapy (with a therapist of the court or of the father's choosing) they will
not only lose custody of their children but will be denied all access to
them

--- Sentence/end 
i: 33
r# 4143

--- Paragraph/end 
i: 5
y: N/A


