i: 6
r# 4145


--- Sentence/start
i: 34
r# 4145

p: .
t: The question most people ask when a family court places a child in the
custody of an abusive parent is how could this happen? Therapists, attorneys, mothers, grandparents, media, and members of the public often
ask the same question


--- Sentence/switch
i: 35
r# 4382

p: .
t:  As you will read in the case studies presented in
this book, mothers often come to court with multiple medical records
documenting spousal abuse and sexual abuse of their children by the
father, only to have the court disregard or minimize the evidence


--- Sentence/switch
i: 36
r# 4637

p: .
t:  Survivors of violence expect to find relief with the court


--- Sentence/switch
i: 37
r# 4698

p: .
t:  Too often they
find the opposite


--- Sentence/switch
i: 38
r# 4733

p: .
t:  Let me begin by giving my perspective on this tragedy
which very much aligns with a major theme of this book


--- Sentence/switch
i: 39
r# 4844

p: .
t: 
My perspective is anecdotal based upon my decades' long practice of representing
abused partners


--- Sentence/switch
i: 40
r# 4944

p: 
t:  These are my observations:

--- Sentence/end 
i: 40
r# 4975

--- Paragraph/end 
i: 6
