i: 7
r# 4977


--- Sentence/start
i: 41
r# 4977

p: .
t: Many judges and other court personnel do not or cannot grasp how
widespread intimate partner abuse and child sexual abuse is


--- Sentence/switch
i: 42
r# 5102

p: .
t:  They do not
understand how widespread misogyny is either


--- Sentence/switch
i: 43
r# 5161

p: .
t:  In the United States, women
and girls live in a culture where any man feels entitled to challenge them


--- Sentence/switch
i: 44
r# 5266

p: .
t: 
Recently I was boarding an airline when I came to my row


--- Sentence/switch
i: 45
r# 5324

p: .
t:  As I proceeded to enter, an elderly White man, who occupied the row's aisle seat,
patronizingly asked me if I was sure I had the right row


--- Sentence/switch
i: 46
r# 5465

p: .
t:  I could not wait
to see if he would ask the person who would occupy the middle seat the
same question


--- Sentence/switch
i: 47
r# 5569

p: .
t:  He did not


--- Sentence/switch
i: 48
r# 5582

p: .
t:  That passenger was young and male


--- Sentence/switch
i: 49
r# 5618

p: .
t:  I was, of
course, tempted to lean over and ask why he had not asked our seatmate
the same question he directed toward me


--- Sentence/switch
i: 50
r# 5741

p: .
t:  But to do so would involve an
innocent stranger in\mdash{}literally\mdash{}the middle of a dispute that would not
change anyone


--- Sentence/switch
i: 51
r# 5871

p: .
t:  I relay this story to describe the everyday harassment of
women when going about living their lives


--- Sentence/switch
i: 52
r# 5973

p: .
t:  Most cisgender men do not
understand how pervasive misogyny is and the depth of its impact


--- Sentence/switch
i: 53
r# 6066

p: .
t:  These
occurrences happen even more frequently with Black, Indigenous, and
People of Color (BIPOC) women


--- Sentence/switch
i: 54
r# 6172

p: .
t:  Protective mothers (and/or their children) experience not only this everyday misogyny but abuse by their
intimate partner


--- Sentence/switch
i: 55
r# 6300

p: .
t:  I wager that most protective mothers have experienced
levels of domestic abuse\mdash{}or their children have\mdash{}far beyond what most
can imagine


--- Sentence/switch
i: 56
r# 6451

p: .
t:  When mothers approach the courts for relief, they do not
realize that they have entered legal institutions that will be emotionally
abusive toward them at an unexpected level


--- Sentence/switch
i: 57
r# 6628

p: .
t:  Courts are not a safe space
for protective mothers

--- Sentence/end 
i: 57
r# 6681

--- Paragraph/end 
i: 7
