r# 8162

p: .
t: Then there are others


--- Sentence/switch
i: 70
r# 8184

p: .
t:  A minority, but devastatingly effective, number
of judges are misogynists


--- Sentence/switch
i: 71
r# 8260

p: .
t:  Changing them is not a matter of training


--- Sentence/switch
i: 72
r# 8304

p: .
t: 
They are the judges who, for whatever reason, cannot attend a training or
are skeptical of everything taught because they know better. You don't
see what I see is a common response


--- Sentence/switch
i: 73
r# 8494

p: .
t:  Judges of all genders ignore abuse,
even child sexual abuse, with impunity


--- Sentence/switch
i: 74
r# 8571

p: .
t:  We do not, and will not, know
how many judges are influenced by their own childhood experiences


--- Sentence/switch
i: 75
r# 8669

p: .
t: 
But we cannot linger on the why of biases against women and children
and biases in favor of fathers


--- Sentence/switch
i: 76
r# 8774

p: .
t:  The intent or lack of it does not change
the fact that mothers are being banned from seeing their children based
upon the testimony of abusers and their so-called experts

--- Sentence/end 
i: 76
r# 8947

