--- Sentence/start
i: 77
r# 8949

p: .
t: I have long been puzzled why judges refuse to accept the high likelihood that men who abuse their intimate partners will abuse their
children


--- Sentence/switch
i: 78
r# 9091

p: .
t:  As a former judge likes to say, if we knew there was a 50 percent
chance that a bank would be robbed, the police would be all over it. But
where the chance of an abusive partner abusing a child is a minimum of
50 percent, institutional actors do not take any preventative action


--- Sentence/switch
i: 79
r# 9380

p: .
t:  That
percentage goes even higher depending upon the frequency and type of
abuse


--- Sentence/switch
i: 80
r# 9462

p: .
t:  Abusing children is a way of continuing to torture the children's
mother


--- Sentence/switch
i: 81
r# 9537

p: .
t:  A double-header in the world of abusers

--- Sentence/end 
i: 81
r# 9579

--- Paragraph/end 
i: 10
y: N/A


