--- Sentence/start
i: 82
r# 9581

p: .
t: Then there are those judges who are abusive themselves


--- Sentence/switch
i: 83
r# 9636

p: .
t:  Barely listening to women in court, discounting their stories, verbally abusing
them, and rejecting children's narratives


--- Sentence/switch
i: 84
r# 9760

p: .
t:  For whatever reason, these
judges reject the reality of children who are abused and instead order
reunification therapy which continues the harm


--- Sentence/switch
i: 85
r# 9911

p: .
t:  Asking children to
participate in the lives of the parent who hurts them is akin to telling
those children that adults are not concerned about their disclosures, including their pleas for help


--- Sentence/switch
i: 86
r# 10106

p: .
t:  Compounding the harm, the non-abusive
parent, who may be the one person that the children trust, is removed
from contact with them

--- Sentence/end 
i: 86
r# 10239

