r# 10241

p: .
t: From my experience as a family law practitioner, I have seen that sexual abuse of female children happens early on when fathers abuse their
daughters


--- Sentence/switch
i: 88
r# 10391

p: .
t:  That is, even if there was no abuse prior to the parents' separation, sexual abuse of daughters happens quite soon after separation


--- Sentence/switch
i: 89
r# 10525

p: .
t: 
This is not to discount the sexual, and other, abuse of boys


--- Sentence/switch
i: 90
r# 10587

p: .
t:  If the abusive
parent is not sexually abusing the boys per se, exposure to pornography
or verbal abuse with disturbing messages on being manly are, nonetheless, common components of a father's abuse of his male children


--- Sentence/switch
i: 91
r# 10813

p: .
t:  The
depravity of sexual abuse of children seemingly has no bottom


--- Sentence/switch
i: 92
r# 10881

p: .
t:  I have
had a few cases where fathers of very young girls provided other men
access to their daughters


--- Sentence/switch
i: 93
r# 10985

p: .
t:  Just imagine how courts would respond to
these allegations, particularly if the basis of the allegations is solely the
testimony of the child? Fortunately, my clients had sufficient evidence
of abuse by the father to convince the judge to prohibit all access to the
child without disclosing this additional information


--- Sentence/switch
i: 94
r# 11306

p: .
t:  Part of the evidence
in one case included psychiatric reports from the daughter's repeated
psychiatric hospitalizations


--- Sentence/switch
i: 95
r# 11428

p: .
t:  Practically speaking, had we addressed the
additional facts of the father making the child sexually available to other
men this could have been detrimental to our case


--- Sentence/switch
i: 96
r# 11598

p: .
t:  Even the sympathetic
judge might view such information as going a step too far and reexamine the mother's reliability as a reporter


--- Sentence/switch
i: 97
r# 11732

p: .
t:  Fortunately for my clients,
the judges who heard these cases were not skeptical of the mother's
intentions


--- Sentence/switch
i: 98
r# 11841

p: .
t:  Importantly, those cases pre-dated the era where claims of
parental alienation saturate every case involving protective mothers


--- Sentence/switch
i: 99
r# 11971

p: .
t:  Yet
the dilemma remains the same: how much information to reveal in court;
and the timing of such revelations is the purview of client and counsel
and must be calculated strategically


--- Sentence/switch
i: 100
r# 12157

p: .
t:  This is no doubt an important topic
for domestic abuse survivors and their advocates to discuss throughout
the case


--- Sentence/switch
i: 101
r# 12275

p: .
t:  As you will read in the comprehensive case studies provided in
this book, sometimes what is presented to the court is deemed wholly
irrelevant if the judge is hostile to the mother

