p: .
t: Parental alienation arguments in all their forms (Parental Alienation
Syndrome [PAS], Parental Alienation [PA], Resist and Refuse Dynamics
[R-RD]) is pervasive in family court and often effective in grossly undermining a mother's claim of abuse


--- Sentence/switch
i: 103
r# 12705

p: .
t:  The mother is further punished with
court orders assigning custody to the abuser and often loss of all visitation privileges with her child


--- Sentence/switch
i: 104
r# 12847

p: .
t:  As Neustein and Lesher discuss, Professor
Joan S


--- Sentence/switch
i: 105
r# 12898

p: .
t:  Meier is a leading researcher who has debunked the so-called
science behind alienation. Although there is no question that some
parents attempt to drive a wedge between their children and the other
parent, that behavior is different than the situations that are described
in this book


--- Sentence/switch
i: 106
r# 13189

p: .
t:  However, when allegations of child abuse arise in a case
where alienation is claimed by the alleged abuser, the court should focus on the domestic violence and child abuse claims, disregarding the
alienation claims


--- Sentence/switch
i: 107
r# 13410

p: .
t:  Abuse and alienation do not happen simultaneously


--- Sentence/switch
i: 108
r# 13462

p: .
t: 
Raising alienation claims against the non-abusive parent is part of a pattern of abuse and should be explored as such


--- Sentence/switch
i: 109
r# 13581

p: .
t:  Reputable psychologists
and psychiatrists have debunked the fundamental notions of alienation


--- Sentence/switch
i: 110
r# 13677

p: .
t: 
Significant science-based organizations do not accept it as a theory,
let alone as a disorder


--- Sentence/switch
i: 111
r# 13772

p: .
t:  The authors of this book address this topic in
depth

--- Sentence/end 
i: 111
r# 13827

