r# 13829

p: .
t: Fundamentally, alienation claims depend upon two myths about wo\-men


--- Sentence/switch
i: 113
r# 13898

p: .
t: 
As mentioned earlier, one is that women lie


--- Sentence/switch
i: 114
r# 13945

p: .
t:  The second is that
women particularly lie about abuse


--- Sentence/switch
i: 115
r# 14001

p: .
t:  Not surprisingly, such stereotypes
were created by men to protect themselves and other men


--- Sentence/switch
i: 116
r# 14094

p: .
t: 
Nevertheless, it is important to remember that not all men are abusive


--- Sentence/switch
i: 117
r# 14166

p: .
t:  By far, abusive men are in the minority


--- Sentence/switch
i: 118
r# 14208

p: .
t:  But abusive men are good
at what they do


--- Sentence/switch
i: 119
r# 14251

p: .
t:  They know, and are groomed in, how to disparage
women and children and how to undermine their targets' credibility


--- Sentence/switch
i: 120
r# 14368

p: .
t: 
Overcoming stereotypes of women scorned, women are crazy, and
women lie is not easy


--- Sentence/switch
i: 121
r# 14465

p: .
t:  These stereotypes are so embedded in our culture that ridding the public, as well as judges and other court staff, of
these biases can be a slow and difficult process


--- Sentence/switch
i: 122
r# 14634

p: .
t:  We expect a higher
level of understanding from judges, but often it is up to the protective
mother to educate the judge


--- Sentence/switch
i: 123
r# 14756

p: .
t:  This is a complex process, particularly if
one cannot afford an expert witness


--- Sentence/switch
i: 124
r# 14837

p: .
t:  Judges hear from abusers' experts
and guardians ad litem railing about the mother's failures


--- Sentence/switch
i: 125
r# 14932

p: .
t:  Judges are
not social scientists


--- Sentence/switch
i: 126
r# 14967

p: .
t:  Without experts for the protective mother, and an
attorney who understands how to attack the father's experts, judges will
not have an adequate record on which to make an informed decision


--- Sentence/switch
i: 127
r# 15158

p: .
t: 
This second edition of this book provides more information for judges
and protective mothers and their advocates to understand abuse, and the
biases that subject protective mothers to further abuse through the legal
process

--- Sentence/end 
i: 127
r# 15383

