--- Sentence/start
i: 128
r# 15385

p: .
t: Finally, I must consider the failure of law schools to produce lawyers
adequately prepared to advocate for protective mothers


--- Sentence/switch
i: 129
r# 15511

p: .
t:  Statistically we
know that at least one in four cases handled by family law attorneys will
involve abuse


--- Sentence/switch
i: 130
r# 15618

p: .
t:  I am not aware of any law school that requires courses
in domestic abuse to be a pre or co-requisite to studying family law


--- Sentence/switch
i: 131
r# 15744

p: .
t: 
Often family law casebooks have just one section devoted to the study
of domestic violence


--- Sentence/switch
i: 132
r# 15836

p: .
t:  Without incorporating the study of abuse and
its legal consequences, students graduate with an incomplete education for representing domestic abuse survivors and their children


--- Sentence/switch
i: 133
r# 16015

p: .
t:  This
makes family law practitioners more vulnerable to believing allegations
of alienation


--- Sentence/switch
i: 134
r# 16108

p: .
t:  As such they lack the tools to adequately defend the protective mother and may not have the energy to mount an aggressive
defense because they believe alienation is real, even in cases where abuse
has occurred


--- Sentence/switch
i: 135
r# 16320

p: .
t:  In essence, law schools are inadvertently setting up their
graduates for incompetent representation of their clients in family cases


--- Sentence/switch
i: 136
r# 16455

p: .
t: 
Malpractice alone should motivate family law attorneys and students to
learn about the alienation smokescreen, the single most effective tool or
strategy preventing protective mothers from keeping their children safe


--- Sentence/switch
i: 137
r# 16673

p: .
t: 
This second edition provides comprehensive case studies of what happens in court to protective mothers


--- Sentence/switch
i: 138
r# 16777

p: .
t:  These narrative case histories need
to be taught in law school


--- Sentence/switch
i: 139
r# 16842

p: .
t:  All things considered, this second edition of
From Madness to Mutiny offers valuable information that attorneys for
protective mothers need to know, and that law students need to learn

